# Every file in this repository is LF -- in the working copy as much as in the index.  HEAD is
# 219/219 LF, and a CRLF working copy is what broke previous tooling here.
#
# The convention used to live only in a README instruction ("clone with core.autocrlf=false").
# That is not a policy: a system-level core.autocrlf=true still rewrote the working copy to CRLF
# on every checkout, and 87 of the 219 tracked files had drifted by the time it was measured.
# Declaring it here puts the rule where no machine setting can override it.
#
# text=auto, not text: binary files must keep their bytes, and only git decides which is which.
* text=auto eol=lf
